<div class="section--tight container">
<div class="prose reveal" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:20px"><p>Small rituals that make a big difference.</p></div>
<div class="steps stagger">
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">01</div><div><h4>Trim before every burn</h4><p>Trim the cotton wick to 1/4 inch before each lighting. This prevents soot, extends burn time, and keeps the flame steady.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">02</div><div><h4>Let it pool edge-to-edge</h4><p>On first burn, allow the wax pool to reach the vessel edge — 2 hours for 8 oz, 3 hours for 13 oz.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">03</div><div><h4>Never burn past 4 hours</h4><p>Longer burns overheat the wax. Extinguish, cool 2 hours, trim wick, then light again.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">04</div><div><h4>Snuff, don't blow</h4><p>Blowing releases smoke. Use a snuffer or dip the wick into the wax pool.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">05</div><div><h4>Store in the dark</h4><p>Keep candles out of direct sunlight when not in use. UV light degrades fragrance.</p></div></div>
</div>
<div class="section-head reveal" style="margin-top:80px"><h2>Caring for your diffuser</h2></div>
<div class="steps stagger">
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">01</div><div><h4>Flip the reeds weekly</h4><p>Flip every 7–10 days for consistent fragrance. More often in warmer rooms.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">02</div><div><h4>Keep away from heat</h4><p>Heat accelerates evaporation. Keep away from radiators, direct sunlight, AC vents.</p></div></div>
<div class="step"><div class="step-num">03</div><div><h4>Replace reeds when scent fades</h4><p>Reeds saturate after 2–3 months. Swap before refilling.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
